Setting a share's flags needs no right.
A share lent without RIGHT_X to hold it to its budget could give itself spare time;
a share's flags change only through a capability to it with RIGHT_X.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call set the flags of a share its caller could not set them on

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -582,9 +582,6 @@ static int op_share(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         return KERR_OK;
     }
     case OP_SHARE_SET: {
-        if (!(cap->rights & RIGHT_X)) {
-            return KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
-        }
         if (arg[1] >= cap->b || (arg[2] & ~(uint32_t)SHARE_SPARE) != 0) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
